      "text": "The AR5 is a medium-altitude, medium-endurance fixed-wing unmanned aircraft designed for intelligence, surveillance, and reconnaissance missions.\n\nIt can remain airborne for up to 20 hours, depending on the payload, and operate beyond line of sight via satellite communications, enabling long-range missions over land and sea.\n\nThe platform supports electro-optical/infrared cameras, synthetic aperture radar, signals intelligence and electronic intelligence sensors, as well as communication relay systems.\n\nIt can also operate from short, unprepared airstrips using automatic takeoff and landing and is designed to function in GPS-denied and electronically contested environments\n\n(Part 3/3)\n\n@medmannews",
